WEBVTT

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.280
I am Kurata Sana, a first year middle school student.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.530
My manager Rei-kun.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.370
Brad, who looks just like a Japanese friend of mine.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.580
Broadway dance director,
Michelle Hamilton.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.670
Her husband is king producer,
Gary Hamilton.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.170
Their only daughter, Sicil.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:55.170
Naozumi-kun's mother, Mizukuchi Yuko who appeared under suspicious circumstances.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.260
The amazing white bat, Babbit.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.680
The ship is leaving the harbor.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.390
My very best friend in New York, Naozumi-kun.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.400
Stupid Mother &
Daughter in America

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.280
Naozumi-kun... Naozumi-kun...

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:33.670
It's all your fault! If anything happens to Naozumi-kun I'm holding you responsible!

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.470
Do you realize what you just said to Naozumi-kun?

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.340
I... just...

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.180
Enough of this nonsense! Come help me find him!

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.200
Sicil is your younger sister.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.280
Naozumi!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.740
I am Gary Hamilton.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.000
Don't say it anymore.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.380
I don't want to know anything anymore.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.270
Naozumi.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:38.860
I want to live alone by myself.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.870
I wish we could be like this forever.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.660
Good-bye!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.580
Naozumi!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.850
It hurts.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.060
My head, it hurts!

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:21.780
I want to go back, go back to Kamura school in Japan.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:26.160
Naozumi-kun!

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.880
Naozumi?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.550
It really is Naozumi!

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.880
What happened to you?
You're completely soaked.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.510
Mom...

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.350
He's not here.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.140
Maybe he went back home?

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:58.770
Hello... Rei-kun, Naozumi-kun, he still hasn't returned?

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.860
Nothing's the matter,
we just lost each other.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.240
I'm fine, I'm with Brad taking cover from the rain.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.740
That's very dangerous, you're right!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.660
If Naozumi-kun comes back,
please tell me, bye.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.540
- Brad?
- What?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.540
What do you mean, 'what'?! Bastard! I'm very angry!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.670
I will never forgive you for all the things you did...

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:21.670
For me...

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.340
Sicil is my everything!

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.170
I'll do anything for Sicil.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.390
I'm the only one who protects Sicil.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.640
Just because of this you use violence and do all these bad things?

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.560
I just wanted to frighten you before, but I could still hurt you whenever I want!

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.520
Your behavior is absolutely wrong!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.770
Wait a minute, I'm too angry,
my face is getting all wrinkled.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:44.070
An actress's face is her life...
I won't yell anymore.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.440
You're the one who's always angry...

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.740
Let's change this ugly face you have on.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.070
No matter what.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:53.870
If anything happens to Naozumi-kun, I will tie you up and throw you into the Ganges River!

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.660
That is a criminal action too.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.370
The Ganges river is here, right here.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.670
Has Naozumi lost his way?

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.340
Ah, yes, he's very stupid.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.340
I'm very worried.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.340
Worried?

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.840
Because it's dark already.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.180
And he didn't bring an umbrella either.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.640
I'm going to look for him.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.640
I'll go too.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.350
Ah! Then I'll...

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.850
...stay and housesit.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.640
I'm becoming worried too.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.650
I hope Sana-chan is all right.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.070
You've become all wishy-washy after coming to New York!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.070
Nothing will happen to Naozumi, right?

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:32.240
Let's wait for him here for a bit.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.790
Hi! I'm Sagami Rei,
are you Naozumi-kun?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.250
Are you Sagami Rei-san?

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.540
Ah yes, this is Sagami Rei.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.380
Um... Are you Naozumi's manager?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.670
I'm his temporary manager.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:48.800
His manager was in the hospital due to food poisoning, but he'd come out soon.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.640
But when he was leaving the hospital, he got hit by an ambulance so now he's back there again.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.560
But, who are you?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.980
I'm Mizukuchi, Yuko Mizukuchi.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:06:59.980
Oh, I see.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:05.150
Naozumi is here at my house, he was soaked in the rain.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.150
He has a fever right now.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.570
Oh, don't worry about him, he's sleeping very well.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.450
Oh, is that so?

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.950
I'm so sorry that he has put a stranger to such trouble.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.750
Ah, but I'm not a stranger.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.460
I'm Naozumi's mother.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.380
Oh, then I have been very rude! Sorry.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.180
Naozumi.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:42.230
I'm Naozumi's mother...

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.190
I'm Naozumi's mother...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.360
Hello? Ah, Rei-kun!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.570
You found him? Is he alright?

00:07:55.570 --> 00:08:00.660
What? Yuko Mizukuchi, his mother?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.870
Was it that person?

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:06.750
Maybe she's Naozumi's real mother.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.840
Hello... Sana-chan, hello...?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.590
Please don't tell anyone about this.
You didn't say anything to Sicil, did you?

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.720
What do you mean, don't bother anymore about it?

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.800
I didn't say anything to Sicil, or to Bernie.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.640
Don't be mad, don't be mad... but still, please don't tell Sicil and them anything.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:23.140
Yes yes, I don't understand this business anyway.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.270
Thank you, Rei-kun.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.770
No problem, bye bye.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.070
So it's alright now. I'm going home.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:35.570
I understand now that you really care about Sicil.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:40.370
But everything you've done so far is wrong.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:46.380
Hurting other people just to protect somebody is an unforgivable thing.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.670
Would a sincere apology help?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.630
You're too naive, you bastard!

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:05.190
Yo Sicil, Bernie!
They've found Naozumi-kun!

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.060
He's safe! You can
come back to supper now.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:10.360
- Sicil.
- Bernie!

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.660
Ah, you're awake?

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.870
I made some hot soup for you.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:27.670
It was lucky that I passed by, you were completely soaked!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.380
How's your temperature?

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.170
Your fever is gone! This is great, I was so worried!

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.470
You just rest, I've already told your manager. Sorry...

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.930
Ah... Naozumi-chan...

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.140
This woman loves to talk!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.770
She's still talking.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.270
How is it? How is the taste?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.110
It's very good.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.870
Sorry, I'm just so happy that...

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:06.660
...you think the soup I made is good.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:15.170
This day... I never even dreamed that this day would arrive.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:27.270
You used to be an actress?

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.940
Not used to, I'm still an actress.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:34.440
I'm negotiating to be in a big Broadway show now!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:39.240
To tell you the truth, I didn't have any luck before, but now everything's going to change.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.370
This person is an actress too?

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:44.660
An actor doesn't mean a foreigner.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.450
Are they a mother-son acting pair?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:48.460
We can't let you become feverish again, so you just lie here some more.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:51.040
You should sleep through the night to morning.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.460
If there are any problems just tell me, don't be too polite.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.460
Good night, Naozumi.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.340
Um...

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.260
What is it?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:05.470
Is my father...

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:07.980
...Gary Hamilton?

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:21.030
{parte b}

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.570
Who told you this?

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:26.580
I found out by accident.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.750
Is he my father?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.500
Y-Yes.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:43.050
We met when he came to Japan to work.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:46.560
Then we fell in love.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.770
At that time he was... very gentle.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:56.940
If at that time
he had stayed with me...

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:01.860
I used to think maybe I wouldn't have left you.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:05.160
I was selfish, and hated him for it.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:08.200
It was all my fault.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:15.920
But now I am very grateful to him.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:23.180
He knew that you had became a very famous child actor in Japan.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.260
Maybe it was because of this that he asked you to work here.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:30.140
Because of this also, I finally met you.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:34.560
Please don't hate him.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.650
I don't hate him anymore, either.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.870
This week's useful English word.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.040
trick = scheme

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.170
Thank you very much for taking care of Naozumi-kun.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:00.750
What are you saying? I'm his mother, I should be the one thanking you.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.670
May I enquire... whose mother are you?

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:04.680
Hi.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.340
Hi.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.850
I am so embarrassed.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.560
As long as you're safe, everything's fine.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:13.060
Sorry, I made you worried.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:17.810
This is the place that you meant to come to, right?

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:22.780
No... she just passed by and saw me.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:31.450
She said that Gary-san was...

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.160
He's your father?

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.040
Yes, she told me so.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.380
So Sicil is my younger sister.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:46.050
So many things just happened, my mind was so confused.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.260
That's why I got a fever.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.850
Naozumi-kun is so naive.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.470
Eh, what do you mean?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.560
Another word for it is 'innocent'.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.480
You're talking like you're superior to everyone again.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.860
I'm not being superior,
just praising you...

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.070
I'm saying you're innocent, like a little child.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.940
You're a child too!

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.740
Of course I'm not... so please don't think like that.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.370
Maybe I should say 'romantic' or 'idiotic' ...

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.660
She's still talking like that ...

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.660
Close it.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.660
Please don't tell Sagami-san and Bernie about Sicil.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.870
Of course I won't say anything.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.540
Thank you.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:24.800
I want to stay here for now.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:29.180
There's a lot of things I must think about.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.350
That's true, that's true.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.140
About the lessons...

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.140
About that...

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.470
Can I sing a song?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.350
Please do.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.060
1,2,1,2,3,5!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:42.270
5, face so red.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.570
One must rest when one's in a fever.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.650
So that's settled.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:47.650
I've helped out!

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.740
I will tell Michelle-san.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.570
I'm very sorry.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.870
Kida baba.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.580
Kida baba is 'no problem' in Chinese.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.960
She keeps on telling me that she's his mother.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.960
Oh yes, she's Naozumi-kun's mother.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.960
Ah, so that is the case.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.260
I'm late! I'm leaving now.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.970
Please work hard!

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:11.970
I see. So Naozumi-kun's mother is in New York.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:18.560
One is nearly late, the other has a cold and needs to rest.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:22.060
This is how children without any professional ambitions act like, full of trouble.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.650
Let's begin practice.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.440
Can't you talk peacefully and be nice for once, lady?

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.570
But I'm used to it now.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:32.200
But the reason Michelle-san is so cold to us

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:36.330
might be because of Gary-san and Naozumi-kun's relationship.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.750
It seems worthy of pity.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.660
A missed beat there!

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:42.670
Yes.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:43.960
I'm home.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.460
Welcome home.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.960
Where's Naozumi?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:52.760
He's still feverish,
so he's staying at Yuko-san's.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.850
Oh yes, Yuko-san is the woman who saved Naozumi-kun.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:57.560
Sicil!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:58.560
Sicil!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.770
She was longing for Naozumi to come back.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:05.270
Naozumi is her only support right now.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.530
Sicil.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:10.280
Yes?

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:12.240
Can I sit next to you?

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.570
Please do.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:21.460
This is the first time that we two can be quiet and just talk.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.880
Naozumi is tired of me.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.460
Because he's always trying to avoid me.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.340
I tried so hard to see him at the mansion, but he left immediately.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.970
I come here and he leaves again.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:37.970
Naozumi is trying to avoid me,
he's sick of me.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.770
Everyone seems to hate me.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:45.270
Naozumi, Papa and Mama all hate me.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:52.440
A child who cannot dance... so... I am a child that no one wants.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:59.540
That time I fell from the stage, my leg tendon snapped.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:05.920
Ever since then, the way Mama and Papa look at me has changed.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.630
It's like they're saying from far away,
'what an annoying child'.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:13.170
'We don't want you' -
that's what their eyes say.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:17.180
Other people's children learn dancing from Mama.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:20.560
Other people's children dance
on Papa's stage.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:26.270
They... All they're interested in is other people's children.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:32.650
I can only look at them. I'm so sad.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.860
Why was I born in such a home?

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:39.370
I am only a child whom no one wants.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:47.870
You hit my head!

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.040
No crying!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:52.880
This is the first time I've ever seen such a spoiled girl like you.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:57.970
Are you going to be like a maggot, indecisive forever?

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:58.970
Maggots = larva of flies, etc, born in rotten meat, etc

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.220
What are maggots?

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:02.430
Don't ask me, I'm disgusted just thinking about it.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.310
So don't mention it!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:08.650
Life is so long, there are times we all act like maggots because we're just people.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:09.690
Maggots?

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.730
Please don't teach
bad things, black Babbit

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.570
Maggots... are like this.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:12.650
Don't look!

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:17.110
Naozumi-kun right now has problems bigger than mountains,

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.240
and he's trying to solve them.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:23.120
That's probably why he no longer has any energy.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:29.460
He probably wants to return to being as strong as he used to be.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.380
Naozumi-kun has always worked hard to help himself.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:38.050
So I think that this time,
he can help himself too.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.970
It'll be ok.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.850
If there comes a time that it isn't enough, we're still here for him, aren't we?

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:46.980
There's me, there's you.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:51.360
When that time comes, let's hope that you won't be worried over ridiculous things.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.650
Ridiculous things?

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:56.280
Yes, Naozumi-kun hasn't said that he's annoyed with you.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.150
Your mama and papa haven't said they didn't want you.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:03.780
But you still think like this...
Isn't that ridiculous?

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:07.160
Mama said that to me once.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.870
It was when she knew that I would never dance again.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:14.170
Why? Why does a thing like this happen to my child?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:17.050
I don't want a child who cannot dance, I don't want her!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:20.220
Don't talk anymore, Michelle.
What if Sicil hears?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:24.140
Michelle Hamilton's child isn't allowed to not be able to dance.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.470
Michelle!

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:31.190
What a dumb mother-daughter pair, how appropriate for New York!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:33.770
To tell you the truth...

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:39.240
Naozumi-kun is just like me...

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:43.370
...abandoned when we were babies.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.450
Abandoned, thrown away.

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:50.750
However, however...

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:57.960
Neither of us ever thought of ourselves as children whom no one wanted.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.340
Even though many things happen every day...

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:06.970
...to slowly shape our laughing, crying, angry, loving-to-live selves.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:12.060
And there are a lot of people who love us too.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.560
Aren't you just the same?

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:22.240
There must be a lot of people who like you.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.070
Just like the way you like Naozumi-kun.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.670
All the things you've done were wrong!

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.760
Hurting other people
just to protect somebody...

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.970
...is an unforgivable thing.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.350
Damn it!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.060
Hi, Brad.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:50.350
Wh-what's that?

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.640
Chicken-and-potato sandwiches.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.150
I don't want any. I don't want your pity.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.060
I don't pity you in the least.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:00.280
I'm just in a good mood.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.740
Here, eat them, I made extras.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.740
The world is not so bad.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:11.240
What weird nonsense
is that guy talking about?

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.840
Are you Gary Hamilton?

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.680
Yes, I am, who are you?

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.350
I'm not a suspicious person.

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.350
I'm Rick, from the pizza shop.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.640
I haven't ordered any pizza.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:36.350
The pizza at our shop tastes really bad, don't ever order from there!

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:37.940
Then how can I help you?

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.860
Only you can help us, Hamilton-san.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.780
Please, would you stop Yuko?

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:44.950
Yu...?

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.740
Yuko Mizukuchi.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:49.570
Naozumi Kamura is at her place right now.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:50.450
What?

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:56.540
She is about to make a serious mistake.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.040
